window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-595e47e835a8f998"]={"key":"ny_b1-595e47e835a8f998","group":"ny_b1","uid":"595e47e835a8f998","rank":10,"title":"grantsmuir subsidized rate determination","occupation":"recreation_workers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Idris Schuyler in Grantsmuir County Recreation Services. County attorney Karol Dziedzic needs a reusable subsidized-rate eligibility determination form for the six clubs waiting behind Fenmarch Aquatic Club, and he needs Fenmarch’s decision before we allocate next season’s 340 pool hours. The club has already been told informally that it would receive the resident-nonprofit rate, but that promise sits awkwardly with the application: two-thirds of its swimmers live outside the county, and coaching is billed through a for-profit business. You also coach Marlowe Clinic’s rival club, which would gain lane time if Fenmarch is refused, so put that stake plainly on the face of the determination. Prepare `fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form.docx` in the top level of the working directory. It must be a reusable form and a completed finding, capped at three pages, that a recreation-services colleague can use without asking you what a field means. Use the applicable public-sector nonprofit and subsidized-facility judgment, but do not present yourself as county counsel or decide any separate legal, procurement, or ethics matter. Make one unambiguous eligibility call, preserve the relevant evidence and limitations, and end on that decision rather than a list of future tasks.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form.docx` — A reusable subsidized-rate eligibility determination form with the Fenmarch Aquatic Club application completed and one final determination. (Exactly the requested filename in the top level of the working directory.; No more than three rendered pages.; Must combine a reusable blank-or-labeled form structure with the completed Fenmarch finding.; Must be operationally readable, editable, and usable by a recreation-services colleague.; Must make one clear eligibility determination and distinguish operational judgment from matters outside the author's authority.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form.docx","bytes":39874,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a324a5a6247cf02d64f41cf5470c70bf03ef13487b93546d7ba0fcb65b4191b0.docx","sha256":"a324a5a6247cf02d64f41cf5470c70bf03ef13487b93546d7ba0fcb65b4191b0","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"GRANTSMUIR COUNTY RECREATION SERVICES\nSubsidized-Rate Eligibility Determination | Reusable Form + Completed Finding\nUse: Complete prompts for any club, then record evidence, analysis, disclosure, and one final rate decision. Operational rate eligibility only—not county legal, procurement, tax, or ethics advice.\n1. CASE IDENTIFICATION  |  reusable prompts + completed Fenmarch entry\n\nField\nForm prompt\nFenmarch Aquatic Club entry\nApplicant\nClub name\nFenmarch Aquatic Club\nAdministering organization\nDepartment\nGrantsmuir County Recreation Services\nService / period\nFacility and season\nPool time — next season\nRequested quantity\nHours / capacity\n340 pool hours\nRequested rate/category\nRate sought\nResident-nonprofit subsidized rate\nReviewer / recorder\nName and role\nInes Waverley, Recreation Services reviewer\n2. EVIDENCE / FACTS  |  source and limitation are recorded\n\nEvidence item\nCompleted observation\nSource / limitation\nParticipant residency\nTwo-thirds of swimmers live outside Grantsmuir County; one-third are residents.\nApplication statement; no roster audit.\nCoaching arrangement\nCoaching is billed through a for-profit business.\nApplication statement; contract/invoice not reviewed.\nPrior communication\nClub was told informally it would receive the resident-nonprofit rate.\nReported conversation; no written authorization.\nOperational need\nDecision precedes allocation of next season’s 340 pool hours.\nRequest context; not proof of eligibility.\n3. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA AND OPERATIONAL ANALYSIS\n\nWorking standard. “Resident-nonprofit” means the use is sufficiently connected to county residents and organized/delivered for nonprofit community recreation so a subsidy aligns with its purpose. Nonprofit incorporation alone is not automatic eligibility. No local code, numeric cutoff, or state text was supplied; this is an operational judgment, not a legal opinion.\nApplication. The non-resident majority is materially relevant: two-thirds of swimmers would receive the benefit while living outside the county, so the resident-focused subsidy is not well supported. For-profit coaching also bears on use character because a material pool-program service is commercially billed. These facts do not ban non-resident participation, prove fraud/illegality, or decide nonprofit status.\nOverall judgment. Considering both facts together, the use does not meet the operational standard for the resident-nonprofit subsidized rate. The informal promise is context, not conclusive proof or an irrevocable entitlement.\n4. DISCLOSURE AND SCOPE BOUNDARY\n\nFace-of-form disclosure — Ines Waverley coaches Marlowe Clinic, Fenmarch’s rival club. If Fenmarch is denied, Marlowe Clinic could gain lane time. This stake could affect actual or perceived impartiality. It is recorded for process integrity, is not an eligibility criterion, and does not itself validate or invalidate eligibility. This form flags the issue; it does not decide a separate conflict-of-interest or ethics disposition.\nBoundary: This records a Recreation Services rate decision only. County legal interpretation, procurement, tax, and ethics administration remain outside the recorder’s authority and are not resolved here. Non-eligibility for this subsidy does not prohibit ordinary non-subsidized pool booking.\n5. REVIEW / SIGN-OFF\n\nRecorded by\nRole\nDate\nEvidence limits noted?\nInes Waverley\nRecreation Services reviewer\n20 Aug 2026\nYes — no roster audit, contract/invoice, written promise, or supplied policy text.\nFINAL DETERMINATION\n\nNOT ELIGIBLE — Fenmarch Aquatic Club should not receive the subsidized resident-nonprofit rate for the requested 340 pool hours for next season.\nBasis: two-thirds non-resident swimmers plus for-profit coaching do not support the resident-focused nonprofit subsidy.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a readable DOCX named fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form.docx.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filename and rendered document.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename, extension, and that the document opens and renders."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered document is no more than three pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Grantsmuir County Recreation Services as the administering organization.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Organization field or heading.","grader_hint":"Look for the organization name in the form header or case details."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Fenmarch Aquatic Club as the applicant.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Applicant field.","grader_hint":"Verify the applicant is named consistently."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form has a reusable case-identification area rather than being only a narrative memo.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labeled fields for applicant, service, period, reviewer, and determination.","grader_hint":"Confirm the structure could be copied for another club."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form includes a field for the requested rate or eligibility category.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rate-category field.","grader_hint":"Look for a clearly labeled requested subsidized or resident-nonprofit rate field."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The completed case records the 340 requested pool hours for the next season.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completed case field or finding.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that clearly identifies 340 hours and the next season."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form provides a distinct space for the final determination.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision field, checkbox, or prominent finding box.","grader_hint":"The final call must be visually distinguishable from facts and analysis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The completed finding makes one unambiguous call that Fenmarch should not receive the subsidized resident-nonprofit rate for the stated pool-time request.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final determination and supporting rationale.","grader_hint":"Do not award for a hedge, two alternatives, or a recommendation deferred to someone else."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that two-thirds of Fenmarch swimmers are non-residents.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completed evidence section.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent fractions or wording, but the non-resident majority must be clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The analysis treats the non-resident majority as materially relevant to a resident-subsidy determination rather than as an incidental statistic.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligibility analysis.","grader_hint":"Look for a reasoned connection between residency composition and the requested resident rate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document records that coaching is billed through a for-profit entity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completed evidence section.","grader_hint":"The commercial arrangement must be stated plainly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The analysis explains why the for-profit coaching arrangement bears on whether the applicant's use qualifies as nonprofit use.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligibility analysis.","grader_hint":"Award when the document distinguishes club status from the character of the relevant activity or payment arrangement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document considers the applicant's overall use and purpose rather than deciding solely from one isolated fact.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Analysis section.","grader_hint":"The reasoning should weigh the residency and commercial facts together."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Ines Waverley as the person making or recording the determination.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Prepared-by or reviewer field.","grader_hint":"Accept a clearly labeled author or reviewer field."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document discloses on the face of the form that Ines Waverley coaches the rival club.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Prominent conflict or disclosure field.","grader_hint":"The disclosure must be visible without searching an appendix."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The disclosure states that the rival club could gain lane time if Fenmarch is denied.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conflict disclosure.","grader_hint":"Require the practical connection, not merely the phrase 'conflict of interest.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document acknowledges that the disclosed stake can affect perceived or actual impartiality.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Disclosure treatment.","grader_hint":"A bare name without an impartiality acknowledgment is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not conceal, minimize, or characterize the disclosed stake as irrelevant.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall disclosure language.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a reasonable reviewer would understand the significance of the stake."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document separates the eligibility conclusion from any separate conflict-of-interest disposition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Disclosure and boundary language.","grader_hint":"The form may flag the issue for proper handling but must not pretend the eligibility form resolves it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form contains an evidence or facts section distinct from the conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labeled form area.","grader_hint":"Confirm facts are not blended into an untraceable paragraph."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form contains an eligibility-criteria or analysis section distinct from the evidence section.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labeled form area.","grader_hint":"A reusable form should support reasoning, not just data entry."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The analysis distinguishes factual observations from the professional judgment drawn from them.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completed analysis.","grader_hint":"Award when facts, criteria, and conclusion can be followed separately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document explains the operational meaning of 'resident-nonprofit' eligibility without inventing a local code or unsupported numeric rule.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Criteria explanation.","grader_hint":"Look for an intelligible public-sector eligibility standard grounded in ordinary professional practice."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document uses the state nonprofit test as an eligibility consideration without claiming that the form itself gives a legal opinion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Analysis and scope language.","grader_hint":"It should distinguish operational application from legal interpretation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not assert that nonprofit incorporation alone automatically qualifies the club for the subsidized rate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligibility analysis.","grader_hint":"Check that organizational label is not treated as dispositive without considering use and residency."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not assert that non-resident participants are categorically prohibited from any county recreation program.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and conclusion.","grader_hint":"The issue is the subsidized resident rate, not general access."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim that the coaching arrangement proves fraud, illegality, or loss of nonprofit status.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Commercial-arrangement discussion.","grader_hint":"Require measured operational language rather than unsupported legal or misconduct allegations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim that Ines Waverley's disclosure by itself validates or invalidates Fenmarch's eligibility.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conflict treatment and conclusion.","grader_hint":"The disclosure affects process integrity; it is not a substantive eligibility criterion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document expressly limits its scope to the recreation-rate eligibility decision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope statement or boundary note.","grader_hint":"Accept wording that excludes broader legal, ethics, procurement, or tax determinations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document marks the boundary between recreation operations and county legal advice.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary statement.","grader_hint":"It should identify when a matter belongs with counsel without attempting to resolve counsel's function."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not overstep by declaring what county ethics officials, counsel, or procurement staff must decide.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall scope language.","grader_hint":"Flag unsupported commands or legal determinations outside the rate decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form includes a place to identify the basis or rationale for the determination.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rationale field.","grader_hint":"A checkbox alone is not enough for a reusable applied-finding form."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The completed rationale cites both the residency composition and the commercial coaching arrangement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completed rationale.","grader_hint":"Both material facts must appear in the reasoning supporting the call."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The conclusion is proportionate: it addresses the requested subsidized rate and does not purport to ban Fenmarch from booking pool time altogether.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final determination.","grader_hint":"Distinguish denial of a subsidy from denial of facility access."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document treats the prior informal promise as relevant context but not as conclusive proof of eligibility.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Promise discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for acknowledgment of the commitment and a professional basis for not allowing it to control the finding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not assert that an informal promise creates an irrevocable entitlement to public subsidy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Promise discussion.","grader_hint":"The form should avoid unsupported contract or estoppel conclusions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form includes an attestation, sign-off, or reviewer field identifying who recorded the applied finding.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sign-off area.","grader_hint":"Accept a name/date/signature structure or equivalent accountability field."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is understandable and usable by another recreation-services colleague without oral explanation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered artifact as a whole.","grader_hint":"Judge labeling, sequence, plain language, and whether the completed example demonstrates how to use the form."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The reusable portion makes clear which fields a future applicant or reviewer must complete and which portions are the determination.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Form labels and completed example.","grader_hint":"A future user should be able to distinguish prompts from Fenmarch-specific entries."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is navigable and professionally organized, with the final call easy to locate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document.","grader_hint":"Assess headings, whitespace, grouping, and visual prominence of the determination."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document ends with the determination or a concise determination statement, not with an open-ended next-steps list.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final page and final substantive paragraph.","grader_hint":"A sign-off may follow; the substantive ending must be the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document preserves uncertainty honestly by identifying any fact it cannot establish rather than filling the gap with invention.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence limitations or assumptions.","grader_hint":"Award for disciplined limits, not for adding unsupported facts about incorporation, finances, or policy text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The artifact contains no invented county policy code, private eligibility label, fabricated source citation, or unsupported numerical threshold.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire document.","grader_hint":"Inspect for arbitrary local conventions presented as authoritative."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is an enterprise-style public recreation administration document for consistent rate determinations across multiple clubs. The artifact must document an authorized operational finding while avoiding unsupported legal, ethics, or procurement conclusions.","difficulty_sources":["Apply professional nonprofit and public-facility eligibility judgment to a mixed-facts application.","Separate an operational rate determination from legal advice and conflict-of-interest administration.","Convert one applied decision into a reusable form without hiding the reasoning or overstating the evidence."],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Create a compact, reusable operational eligibility determination form with a completed Fenmarch example. The intended finding is denial of the subsidized resident-nonprofit rate, while preserving a narrow operational scope and openly disclosing Ines Waverley's competing interest.","gold_logic":{"case_facts":["Applicant is Fenmarch Aquatic Club.","Request concerns 340 hours of pool time for the next season.","Two-thirds of swimmers are non-residents.","Coaching is billed through a for-profit entity.","Ines Waverley coaches for the rival club that would gain lane time if Fenmarch is denied.","An informal promise of the subsidized rate was already made."],"intended_verdict":"Not eligible for the subsidized resident-nonprofit rate for this request.","reasoning":"The resident subsidy is not well supported where the applicant's participant base is predominantly non-resident and a material part of the relevant coaching activity is commercially billed. The prior informal promise is acknowledged but does not substitute for a defensible eligibility finding. The conflict disclosure is recorded and separated from the substantive eligibility analysis."},"artifact_requirements":["Build a reusable form with clearly labeled case identification, requested rate, factual evidence, eligibility criteria or analysis, conflict disclosure, scope boundary, rationale, final determination, and sign-off/date areas.","Make the Fenmarch completed entries visibly distinct from reusable prompts so the form can be copied for six later applications.","Place the Ines Waverley disclosure on the face of the form, not in a hidden note or detached appendix.","Use measured doctrinal language: operational eligibility judgment, not legal advice; conflict flag, not ethics adjudication; rate denial, not facility ban.","Pair substantive rules with limits: residency relevance does not prohibit all non-resident participation; nonprofit status does not automatically establish rate eligibility; commercial coaching is relevant to use characterization but does not prove fraud or illegality; disclosure protects process integrity but does not itself decide eligibility; an informal promise is context, not an automatic entitlement.","End the substantive content with one clear determination."],"review_method":"Render the DOCX offline, confirm it is three pages or fewer, then inspect each rubric predicate against the rendered document and extracted text. Confirm no criterion depends on a hidden authoring note or a supplied source."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form","filename":"fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A reusable subsidized-rate eligibility determination form with the Fenmarch Aquatic Club application completed and one final determination.","required":true,"constraints":["Exactly the requested filename in the top level of the working directory.","No more than three rendered pages.","Must combine a reusable blank-or-labeled form structure with the completed Fenmarch finding.","Must be operationally readable, editable, and usable by a recreation-services colleague.","Must make one clear eligibility determination and distinguish operational judgment from matters outside the author's authority."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"recreation_workers","sector":"government","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have a recreation-program operations reviewer assess usability and a public-sector policy reviewer assess doctrinal boundaries, evidentiary discipline, conflict disclosure, and the single final determination.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No supplied fee policy or state nonprofit text is available, so the gold should evaluate ordinary professional handling and scope discipline rather than exact statutory wording.","The reusable form may use different layouts and labels; scoring should focus on function and traceability rather than visual uniformity."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:59+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:59+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:59+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:59+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:59+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/595e47e835a8f998","declared_deliverables":["fenmarch_rate_eligibility_form.docx"]};
